  "reason": "The best result so far is config_042 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.7250. Evidence strongly favors scvi_n200 over scgpt (0.72 vs 0.52), imagenet_vit_l over resnet50, transformer over avgpool, and multiprofile over singleprofile. The only untested RNA encoder in the optimal multimodal setup is pca_n2000. Since this is the final experiment, config_023 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is the best choice: it pairs the only untested RNA encoder with all other components shown to be optimal, reducing residual uncertainty about whether a linear RNA representation could complement the image features in a way the learned encoders do not. While the probability of beating 0.7250 is low given scgpt's poor performance, this is the highest-information and highest-expected-value remaining test, as all other untested configs either use inferior image encoders, aggregations, or profile settings that have already been shown to underperform."
